同时我们也会深入探讨读书俱乐部及其背后的那些戏剧性故事。

23
00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.790
Angela, I believe you did a deep dive on the origins of afternoon tea.
安吉拉，我相信你对下午茶的起源做了深入研究。

24
00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.430
I did.
没错。

25
00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.070
You know I can't wait for that.
你知道我有多期待这个。

26
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.110
It was so fun.
太有趣了。

27
00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:27.070
And Jenna, you've been so excited for this episode because you're a super book nerd, and you've got lots to share.
还有珍娜，你一直很期待这一集，因为你是个超级书呆子，有很多东西要分享。

28
00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.950
Oh, I am in my happy place today.
噢，我今天简直乐在其中。

29
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.170
Cassie, I know you as well.
凯西，我知道你也是。

30
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.750
Yes, this is very true.
是的，这千真万确。

31
00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:33.530
I love reading.
我热爱阅读。

32
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.210
It's not to say that Sam and I don't love reading.
这并不是说萨姆和我不爱读书。

33
00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.450
It's a little harsh, but all right.
这话有点伤人，但好吧。

34
00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:41.810
Did you feel it?
你感觉到了吗？

35
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:42.390
Did you feel it?
你感觉到了吗？

36
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.910
A little smug opening?
开场是不是有点自鸣得意？

37
00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:44.190
Sure.
当然。

38
00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:53.490
Well, as you all know, the Finer Things Club was revealed in Season 4, Episode 10 of The Office, titled Branch Wars.
如大家所知，“高雅事物俱乐部”是在《办公室》第四季第十集《分部之战》中首次亮相的。

39
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:59.390
This episode introduces the club as a very exclusive group within the Scranton branch.
这一集将该俱乐部介绍为斯克兰顿分部内一个非常高级的团体。

40
00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:05.590
It has three members, Pam Beasley, Oscar Martinez, and Toby Flenderson.
它有三名成员：帕姆·比斯利、奥斯卡·马丁内斯和托比·弗兰德森。

41
00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.630
And let me tell you, Toby is not interested in having anyone else join.
而且我得告诉你，托比对让其他人加入一点兴趣都没有。

42
00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.130
No, he is not.
不，他确实没有。

43
00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.010
Well, there are rules for the Finer Things Club.
嗯，“高雅事物俱乐部”是有规矩的。

44
00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.490
It's very organized.
它非常有组织性。

45
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.930
And here's a clip of Pam explaining how it all works.
下面是帕姆解释俱乐部运作方式的片段。

46
00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.070
Oscar, Toby, and I are founding members of the Finer Things Club.
奥斯卡、托比和我，我们是“高雅事物俱乐部”的创始成员。

47
00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:29.330
We meet once a month to discuss books and art, celebrate culture in a very civilized way.
我们每月聚会一次，讨论书籍和艺术，以一种非常文明的方式庆祝文化。

48
00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.770
Sometimes the debate can get heated, but we're always respectful.
有时辩论会变得激烈，但我们始终保持尊重。

49
00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:39.370
There is no paper, no plastic, and no work talk allowed.
这里不允许使用纸质或塑料制品，也不允许谈论工作。

50
00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.330
It's very exclusive.
它非常高级。

51
00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.010
Look at how happy she is.
看她多开心啊。

52
00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.150
It's very exclusive.
这非常排外。

53
00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.990
Just so hoity-toity.
真是太自命不凡了。

54
00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.410
I mean, I think she's just proud of her little group.
我是说，我觉得她只是为她的小团体感到自豪。

55
00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:54.210
I think she is proud, but I also think she's hoity-toity.
我觉得她是自豪，但我也觉得她自命不凡。

56
00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:55.510
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

57
00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:00.950
Well, you know, things are going very well for our little Finer Things Club group until
嗯，你知道，我们“精致事物俱乐部”的小团体一直进行得很顺利，直到

58
00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.330
Andy decides he wants to be a member.
安迪决定他想成为会员。

59
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.730
And then later, Pam lets Jim into the group.
后来，帕姆让吉姆加入了这个团体。

60
00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.710
You know, she feels bad for him.
你知道，她为他感到难过。

61
00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.830
And he's clearly not read the book, Angela's Ashes.
而且他显然没读过那本书，《安琪拉的灰烬》。

62
00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:13.830
Drama.
戏剧性。

63
00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:14.590
Drama.
戏剧性。

64
00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:20.470
And you guys, we were all talking, and we realize any book club we've heard of,
伙计们，我们一直在讨论，我们意识到我们听说过的任何读书俱乐部，

65
00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.590
there's always some drama.
总会有一些戏剧性的事。

66
00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:26.190
And we reached out to you guys, and you wrote in with your book club drama stories,
我们联系了你们，你们写信告诉了我们你们的读书俱乐部戏剧故事，

67
00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.070
and you definitely confirmed our theory.
你们绝对证实了我们的理论。

68
00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.430
For example, we got this letter from Colleen C.
例如，我们收到了这封来自匹兹堡的科琳·C的信，

69
00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.350
in Pittsburgh, which I just loved.
我非常喜欢。

70
00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:35.330
Here it is.
就是这封。

71
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.450
Colleen said,
科琳说，

72
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.470
I attended a snooty book club similar to the Finer Things Club.
我参加过一个类似于“精致事物俱乐部”的势利读书俱乐部。

73
00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:41.910
See?
看吧？

74
00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:42.510
Snooty.
势利。

75
00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:47.410
I was invited by a friend and didn't realize how exclusive it was.
我是被朋友邀请去的，没意识到它有多排外。

76
00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:52.690
They rotated hosts each month, and the host had to provide the food, venue, and drinks.
他们每个月轮换东道主，东道主必须提供食物、场地和饮料。

77
00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:56.730
The host would be silently judged on what they were able to provide,
东道主会因为他们所能提供的东西而被默默评判，

78
00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.670
and if it wasn't up to standards, would be openly critiqued in the group chat.
如果达不到标准，就会在群聊中被公开批评。

79
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.270
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

80
00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

81
00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.290
This is a book club Angela would like.
这是一个安琪拉会喜欢的读书俱乐部。

82
00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.010
Well, she would love the judging.
嗯，她会喜欢这种评判的。

83
00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:08.750
Yes.
没错。

84
00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.870
Colleen said the books selected were long and intellectual.
科琳说选的书都很长且很有深度。

85
00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.690
The discussion was very formal.
讨论非常正式。

86
00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.310
At the end of the night, we would all go around and rate the book from one to five.
晚上结束时，我们会轮流给书打分，从一到五分。

87
00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:25.630
Members were encouraged to be extremely careful in rating a book of five,
鼓励成员在给书打五分时要极其谨慎，

88
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.670
and should only do so if the book had, quote, changed their life.
只有当这本书“改变了他们的人生”时才应该这样做。

89
00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.270
Eventually, the original members decided the book club was getting too big.
最终，原始成员决定读书俱乐部变得太大了。

90
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.970
They were mad that people were just inviting their friends without any sort of vetting process.
他们很生气，因为人们在没有任何审查程序的情况下就邀请了自己的朋友。

91
00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.350
They met together and selected who would be kicked out of the book club.
他们聚在一起，挑选出谁将被踢出读书俱乐部。

92
00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:50.030
All members being kicked out received a formal phone call,
所有被踢出的成员都接到了正式电话，

93
00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.590
letting them know they were no longer welcome to attend.
通知他们不再受欢迎。

94
00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:57.170
I ended up being kicked out, but my friend warned me in advance,
我最终被踢出了，但我朋友提前警告了我，

95
00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.170
and I ignored the call out of spite.
我出于赌气没接那个电话。

96
00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:03.050
They called several times before finally resigning to the fact
他们打了好几次电话，最后不得不接受现实，

97
00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:06.290
that they'd have to inform me of my removal over voicemail.
即他们必须通过语音留言通知我被除名了。

98
00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:11.970
All of us who were kicked out started our own book club with less pressure and less rules.
我们所有被踢出的人都成立了自己的读书俱乐部，压力更小，规则也更少。

99
00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.710
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

100
00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:16.750
So snooty.
太势利了。

101
00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:17.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

102
00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:20.630
Well, you know who has a book club, lady?
好吧，你知道谁有读书俱乐部吗，女士？

103
00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.410
Who has a book club?
谁有读书俱乐部？

104
00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.750
The writer of Branch Wars.
《分部之战》的编剧。

105
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.030
Mindy Kaling.
敏迪·卡灵。

106
00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.670
Oh, yes, of course she does.
哦，是的，她当然有。

107
00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:31.250
And I guess everyone can join her book club, so it's not snooty.
我想任何人都可以加入她的读书俱乐部，所以它并不势利。

108
00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:34.890
I went to the website for it, and this is what it says.
我去了她的网站，上面是这样写的。

109
00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.070
Fresh, vibrant, and binge-worthy reads.
清新、充满活力且让人欲罢不能的读物。

110
00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.010
Mindy's book studio celebrates emerging and diverse voices,
敏迪的图书工作室旨在颂扬新兴和多元化的声音，

111
00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:45.830
from fresh romantic comedies and poignant coming-of-age stories
从清新的浪漫喜剧和深刻的成长故事，

112
00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:49.890
to suspenseful dramas with unforgettable female protagonists.
到拥有令人难忘的女主角的悬疑剧。

113
00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.790
And then there's a quote from Mindy.
然后还有敏迪的一段引言。

114
00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:56.290
It says, I'm passionate about bringing unique stories to readers and viewers,
上面写着，我热衷于为读者和观众带来独特的故事，

115
00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:00.710
and I can't wait to help discover and support talented new voices through Mindy's book studio.
我迫不及待地想通过敏迪的图书工作室去发现并支持有才华的新声音。

116
00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.350
Right now, they're spotlighting eight books, and I'll put them in our stories.
目前，他们正在重点推荐八本书，我会把它们发到我们的快拍里。

117
00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.290
I love this.
我喜欢这个。

118
00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.030
I know.
我知道。

119
00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:14.030
Oh, I love the idea of starting a book club, but the follow-through sounds kind of daunting to me.
哦，我很喜欢创办读书俱乐部的想法，但后续的执行对我来说听起来有点让人望而却步。

120
00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:19.290
Well, lady, I have a little surprise for our office ladies group today.
好吧，女士，今天我为我们的办公室女士小组准备了一个小惊喜。

121
00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.330
Are you starting a book club?
你要创办读书俱乐部吗？

122
00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:25.950
I'm not starting a book club, but I do have a passion for reading.
我不是要创办读书俱乐部，但我确实对阅读充满热情。

123
00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:32.390
Lady, you gave me that amazing book club membership for my birthday from that independent bookstore.
女士，你生日时送了我那家独立书店的超棒读书俱乐部会员资格。

124
00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:39.070
So I thought maybe it would be fun to surprise each of you today with one of my favorite books.
所以我想到今天给你们每人一个惊喜，送你们一本我最喜欢的书，也许会很有趣。

125
00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.630
Oh, that's wonderful.
哦，那太棒了。

126
00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.590
That I have hand-selected for each of you.
这是我为你们每一个人亲手挑选的。

127
00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.790
Oh, so we have a different one?
哦，所以我们每人收到的都不一样？

128
00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:45.390
Yes.
是的。

129
00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.290
Oh, that sounds so cool.
哦，那听起来太酷了。

130
00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.090
Now, this is a book that is a gift to me or a task that I now have to read?
那么，这是一本送给我的礼物，还是我现在必须完成的阅读任务？

131
00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.850
It is a gift.
这是一份礼物。

132
00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:53.230
Okay.
好的。

133
00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:56.410
But Sam, your phrasing says everything.
但是山姆，你的措辞说明了一切。

134
00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:57.650
Yeah, when is this due?
是啊，这书什么时候要读完？

135
00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:00.710
Cassie, turn around.
凯西，转过身去。

136
00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:05.050
