00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:43.840
And I was neck and neck with another reader, and I ended up winning, which was very cool.
我和另一位读者不相上下，最后我赢了，感觉真的很酷。

316
00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:45.660
But also, I felt crazy.
但同时也觉得自己有点疯狂。

317
00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.960
How many books did you read to win this title?
为了赢得这个头衔，你读了多少本书？

318
00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.000
So I read over 66 books last year.
去年我读了超过66本书。

319
00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:52.760
Wow.
哇。

320
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.560
That's more than one a week.
那相当于每周不止一本。

321
00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:54.960
Yeah.
是的。

322
00:13:55.180 --> 00:14:00.080
And some of them, like, you don't get as many points, but you can read like audiobooks or
有些书得分没那么高，但你可以听有声书，或者

323
00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.180
mangas, graphic novels.
看漫画、图像小说。

324
00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:05.700
So I do that a lot on top of reading like a novel.
所以我除了读小说，也会经常看这些。

325
00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:07.500
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

326
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.940
Did you just have so many stories in your head?
你脑子里装得下那么多故事吗？

327
00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.600
Because like when I read, I sit for a while with stuff, you know, and I think about it.
因为我读书的时候，会花时间去消化，你知道的，我会去思考。

328
00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:16.860
Like, how did that feel?
那种感觉怎么样？

329
00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:17.480
Yeah.
嗯。

330
00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:21.760
I think if it was a book I wasn't in love with, I would pick up the pace.
如果那本书我不是特别喜欢，我就会加快阅读速度。

331
00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:26.400
But if I love a book, I will really take my time and sit in it.
但如果我很喜欢一本书，我真的会花时间细细品味。

332
00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:31.580
And I love a Saturday morning reading for a couple hours on the couch with a cat is one
我特别喜欢周六早上在沙发上抱着猫读几个小时书，

333
00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.660
of my favorite things to do.
这是我最喜欢做的事情之一。

334
00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:36.760
So of all the books that you read, is there a favorite?
在你读过的所有书中，有最喜欢的一本吗？

335
00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:42.100
I think in the beginning of the year, I read Octavia Butler for the first time.
年初的时候，我第一次读了奥克塔维娅·巴特勒的作品。

336
00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.880
I really loved the world she built.
我非常喜欢她构建的世界。

337
00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.960
And like, she's from Pasadena, which is really cool, too.
而且她是帕萨迪纳人，这也很酷。

338
00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.840
So I really enjoyed her.
所以我真的很喜欢她。

339
00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:53.000
And I also really like this Japanese detective author.
我还很喜欢一位日本推理小说作家。

340
00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.700
His name's Keigo Higashino, Devotion of Suspect X.
他叫东野圭吾，《嫌疑人X的献身》。

341
00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.800
That's the one that got me into him.
就是那本书让我迷上了他。

342
00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.880
And then I recommended it to my book club.
后来我把它推荐给了我的读书俱乐部。

343
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.680
And like half of them have read it now.
现在有一半的人都读过了。

344
00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:08.180
And I've read like several of his books because they always take place in a different part of Japan.
我已经读了好几本他的书了，因为它们的故事总是发生在不同的日本城市。

345
00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:10.020
And it's really cool.
真的很棒。

346
00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.600
That's so great.
那太好了。

347
00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.160
OK, wait, I have to ask.
等等，我必须问一下。

348
00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.120
So you've been in this book club five years and then you won.
所以你参加这个读书俱乐部五年了，然后你赢了。

349
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:17.620
Yeah.
是的。

350
00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.480
It was neck and neck with another person.
当时我和另一个人竞争非常激烈。

351
00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.440
Was there any book club drama?
读书会有什么八卦吗？

352
00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:22.760
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

353
00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:23.160
Yes.
有。

354
00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:28.820
So like the first year I played, I almost got first place because I was just like,
我第一年参加的时候，差点就拿了第一名，因为我当时觉得，

355
00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.700
oh, this is awesome and I'm reading a whole lot.
哇，这太棒了，而且我读了好多书。

356
00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.580
But then someone who was in second, like, beat me in the last minute.
但后来有个排第二的人，在最后一刻反超了我。

357
00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:38.780
So this year, I like hung back in second place.
所以今年，我特意保持在第二名。

358
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:39.660
On purpose?
故意的？

359
00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:40.540
Like strategy?
是某种策略吗？

360
00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:44.940
Yeah, on purpose because you can kind of see the other people and what they're reading.
对，是故意的，因为你可以看到其他人都在读什么书。

361
00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.280
So I was like clocking what she was reading.
所以我一直在盯着她读什么。

362
00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:50.100
And I was like, oh, I've read way more foreign authors.
我心想，哦，我读的外国作家作品多多了。

363
00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.940
So I'm going to get like a bonus and win.
所以我肯定能拿到额外加分并获胜。

364
00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:57.200
And then like three days before the deadline, she all of a sudden uploaded seven books.
结果在截止日期前三天，她突然上传了七本书。

365
00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.400
Everyone got really mad because they're like, you can't do that.
大家都气坏了，觉得她怎么能这样。

366
00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.020
You can't like hide what you're reading.
你不能藏着自己读的书。

367
00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.520
You have to like have it out in the open.
你必须得公开才行。

368
00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:07.760
And then I like got on a call with the guy who runs it.
然后我给负责这个活动的人打了个电话。

369
00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:08.440
Cassie.
卡西。

370
00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.160
And he's like, I'm so sorry about this.
他说，真的很抱歉发生这种事。

371
00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:11.940
I'm like, it's okay.
我说，没关系。

372
00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.020
I think I can still win.
我觉得我还是能赢。

373
00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:20.720
I think if I just listen to audiobooks for two days straight and do puzzles, I can still win.
我想如果我连续两天不停地听有声书，再做做拼图，我还是能赢。

374
00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:23.000
And that's exactly what I did.
我就是这么做的。

375
00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:24.340
And I won.
然后我赢了。

376
00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:25.780
You were determined.
你真是太有决心了。

377
00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:30.300
Because I knew what it felt like to be in first place and lose at the end.
因为我知道那种身处第一却在最后关头输掉的感觉。

378
00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.560
That I was like, this is driving me insane.
我当时就觉得，这简直要让我疯了。

379
00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:35.980
If I don't win this year, I don't think I'll ever be able to do it again.
如果今年再不赢，我想我以后再也不会参加了。

380
00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:38.300
This year, I'm probably only going to read 10 books.
今年我大概只会读10本书。

381
00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:40.280
And you got that trophy.
而且你还拿到了那个奖杯。

382
00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:43.920
I just gave you a thousand page Stephen King books.
我刚给了你几本斯蒂芬·金的千页巨著。

383
00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:44.500
Yes.
没错。

384
00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.500
That's going to take some time if you decide to dive in.
如果你决定开始读的话，那得花不少时间。

385
00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:48.100
I will.
我会读的。

386
00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:48.480
I will.
我会读的。

387
00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.220
I'm reading something else right now, but I will have it on my shelf.
我现在正在读别的书，但我会把它放在书架上。

388
00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:51.860
Wow.
哇。

389
00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:53.860
See, every book club has some drama.
你看，每个读书会都有点八卦。

390
00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.840
Well, speaking of book club drama and other club drama,
说到读书会的八卦，还有其他俱乐部的八卦，

391
00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.440
thanks to the assistant editor for The Office, Rob Burnett,
多亏了《办公室》的助理编辑罗伯·伯内特，

392
00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:06.440
we have some of the early outlines for the Finer Things Club.
我们拿到了一些“精致事物俱乐部”早期的提纲。

393
00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.340
You told me you found these.
你跟我说你找到了这些。

394
00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:12.520
I did not know about these, so this is going to be a surprise to me.
我之前完全不知道，所以这对我来说也是个惊喜。

395
00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.980
These are just a few little fun nuggets.
这只是几个有趣的小片段。

396
00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:20.260
So the writers had this idea to show a few previous Finer Things Club meetings,
编剧们当时有个想法，想展示几次之前的“精致事物俱乐部”会议，

397
00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:22.360
and this is what it said in the outline.
提纲里就是这么写的。

398
00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:26.060
Oh, we see flashbacks of past meetings.
哦，我们能看到过去会议的闪回。

399
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.800
Michael tries to join.
迈克尔试图加入。

400
00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:31.160
Meredith comes in and loudly slurps from her cup.
梅雷迪思走进来，大声地喝着杯子里的东西。

401
00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:34.580
Pam says they occasionally have guest lecturers.
帕姆说他们偶尔会有客座讲师。

402
00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:39.080
And they see Daryl playing the entertainer for the Jazz Age meeting.
我们看到达里尔在爵士时代会议上扮演娱乐者的角色。

403
00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:44.160
We see Dwight smashing something in the Finer Things meeting out of frustration.
我们看到德怀特在“精致事物俱乐部”会议上因为沮丧而砸东西。

404
00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.080
Wow.
哇。

405
00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.100
So the Finer Things Club had a lot of people come and go.
所以“精致事物俱乐部”来来去去过很多人。

406
00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:54.880
They ultimately didn't settle on any of that other than Pam, Oscar, and Toby, and Andy.
除了帕姆、奥斯卡、托比和安迪，他们最终没有确定其他人选。

407
00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:59.360
But there was possibly some back history to the club.
但这个俱乐部可能还有一些背景故事。

408
00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:00.100
Yeah.
是啊。

409
00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:03.340
I like to wonder how long has this been going on.
我常想这到底持续了多久。

410
00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:03.780
Yeah.
是啊。

411
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:09.280
And I'm sure to Toby's delight that he gets to have these meetings with Pam.
而且我相信托比一定很高兴能和帕姆一起开这些会。

412
00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:09.920
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

413
00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:10.480
Right?
对吧？

414
00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:16.400
But they did sort of toy with, like, how many other office members have at one point been in the club.
但他们确实考虑过，比如还有多少其他办公室成员曾经加入过这个俱乐部。

415
00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:19.940
And we didn't get to see those play out, but I wish we would have.
我们没能看到那些情节展开，但我希望我们能看到。

416
00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:22.240
This is a runner I would have liked to have seen more of.
这是一个我希望能看到更多后续的连贯情节。

417
00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:28.180
I am so sad that we did not revisit the Finer Things Club in the way that we would revisit the party planning committee.
我很遗憾我们没能像重温派对策划委员会那样重温“精致事物俱乐部”。

418
00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:28.520
Yeah.
是啊。

419
00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:34.760
Just somewhere in season nine, if we could have had another meeting, it would have just made me so happy.
只要在第九季的某个地方，如果我们能再开一次会，那一定会让我非常开心。

420
00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:44.460
Well, Angela, when we broke down Branch Wars, you also said that there were some fun deleted scenes about some of the Dunder Mifflin employees' reactions to the Finer Things Club.
嗯，安吉拉，当我们拆解《分部战争》那一集时，你也说过有一些关于邓德·米夫林员工对“精致事物俱乐部”反应的有趣删减片段。

421
00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:51.640
We didn't play them, but I think that since today's episode is dedicated to the Finer Things Club, we should play them today.
我们当时没放，但我觉得既然今天这一集是专门讲“精致事物俱乐部”的，我们今天应该放出来。

422
00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:52.820
Oh, for sure.
哦，当然。

423
00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:53.820
And they're super fun.
而且它们超级有趣。

424
00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.320
They're in the super fan version.
它们在超级粉丝版里。

425
00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:59.280
And I want to start with one that would have happened at the very beginning of the episode.
我想从一个本应发生在这一集开头的情节开始。

426
00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:05.320
Pam is going to walk over to Oscar and ask if he brought his book, A Room with a View, for their meeting that day.
帕姆走过去问奥斯卡有没有带那本《看得见风景的房间》来参加当天的会议。

427
00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.400
And Angela and Kevin are so snarky.
安吉拉和凯文真是太刻薄了。

428
00:19:10.810 --> 00:19:12.930
Oscar, did you bring it?
奥斯卡，你带了吗？

429
00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.410
I don't want to be in.
我不想加入。

430
00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:17.990
His best work.
他的巅峰之作。

431
00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.490
Okay, well, I have the tablecloth.
好吧，我带了桌布。

432
00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:20.490
Don't forget the flatware.
别忘了餐具。

433
00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:21.270
Sure thing, Pam.
没问题，帕姆。

434
00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:21.770
Can't wait.
迫不及待了。

435
00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:22.970
Sure thing, Pam.
没问题，帕姆。

436
00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:24.330
Fru-fru club.
矫情的俱乐部。

437
00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.670
Must be nice.
真好啊。

438
00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:27.190
Look at me.
看看我。

439
00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.870
I wear underwear.
我穿内裤。

440
00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:32.660
My goodness.
天哪。

441
00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:36.140
I know, but Angela mocks Pam.
我知道，但安吉拉在嘲笑帕姆。

442
00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.180
Must be nice.
真好啊。

443
00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:41.780
Well, we're going to hear more about what Angela thinks of the Finer Things Club.
好吧，我们接下来会听到更多安吉拉对“精致事物俱乐部”的看法。

444
00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:46.640
In fact, we have talking heads from Toby, Angela, and Meredith.
事实上，我们有托比、安吉拉和梅雷迪思的采访片段。

445
00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.220
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

446
00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:50.980
I love the Finer Things Club.
我喜欢“精致事物俱乐部”。

447
00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:58.500
My ex-wife used to have a book club, and I would read their book and sometimes listen from the kitchen.
我前妻以前有个读书俱乐部，我会读她们的书，有时还会从厨房偷听。

448
00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:02.600
The Finer Things Club was not sanctioned by the party planning committee.
“精致事物俱乐部”并没有得到派对策划委员会的批准。

449
00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:04.960
Renegade clubs are dangerous.
这种叛逆的俱乐部很危险。

450
00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.460
I squashed the Weight Loss Buddies support group.
我曾经解散过“减肥伙伴”互助小组。

451
00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.300
They didn't need to gather.
他们没必要聚在一起。

452
00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.080
It was just gross.
那真是太恶心了。

453
00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:17.860
I don't know why I'm not in the Finer Arts Club.
我不知道为什么我没能加入“高雅艺术俱乐部”。

454
00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:20.740
It's bullcrap.
简直是胡扯。

455
00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.190
You clean it up.
你自己清理干净。

456
00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:32.310
Yeah, so Meredith is like just slurping out of this big like 7-Eleven Super Gulp, and then she just throws it on the ground.
是啊，梅雷迪思当时正用那种7-Eleven的大杯超大号饮料在那儿吸溜，然后她直接把它扔在了地上。

457
00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:35.250
And then she looks at camera, and she's like, you clean it up.
接着她看向镜头，说，你自己清理干净。

458
00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:41.290
Not really selling yourself, Meredith, to be in the Finer Things Club.
梅雷迪思，你这样可没法让自己加入“高雅艺术俱乐部”。

459
00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:44.290
Clearly, this club ruffled a lot of feathers.
显然，这个俱乐部惹恼了不少人。

460
00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.430
They are definitely not.
他们绝对不是。

461
00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:49.330
I mean, not if Meredith is throwing her beverage on the ground.
我是说，如果梅雷迪思把饮料扔在地上，那肯定不行。

462
00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:49.750
I know.
我知道。

463
00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:53.170
I think it might be time to start sharing some book club dramas, lady.
我觉得是时候分享一些读书俱乐部的八卦了，女士。

464
00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:54.510
Let's do it.
来吧。

465
00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.690
I just love this letter from Lucas G.
我太喜欢卢卡斯·G寄来的这封信了。

466
00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:57.490
in Seattle.
来自西雅图的。

467
00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.450
It took some twists and turns.
它经历了一些转折。

468
00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.330
I was not expecting.
我完全没预料到。

469
00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:04.410
Okay, so we went through the letters you guys sent.
好的，我们看过了你们寄来的信。

470
00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:04.850
Yeah.
没错。

471
00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:08.650
And there was one that I pulled aside, and I said, Jenna, do not read this.
其中有一封我特意挑了出来，我对珍娜说，别看这封。

472
00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:08.930
Yes.
是的。

473
00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:10.130
Because I wanted to read it to you here.
因为我想在这里读给你听。

474
00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.010
This is the one you pulled aside.
这就是你挑出来的那封。

475
00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:16.030
So I have no idea what Lucas wrote in because I purposely didn't read it.
所以我完全不知道卢卡斯写了什么，因为我特意没看。

476
00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:16.550
Correct.
没错。

477
00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:18.130
I can't wait to hear.
我迫不及待想听听了。

478
00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:18.870
All right.
好的。

479
00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:26.410
Lucas said, I have the perfect story to tell about the demise of my book club, which happened almost a year ago.
卢卡斯说，我有一个关于我读书俱乐部解散的绝佳故事，那件事发生在大约一年前。

480
00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:27.370
Demise?
解散？

481
00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:33.010
I never thought a book club meeting would turn into an absolute disaster, but here we are.
我从没想过读书会会变成一场彻底的灾难，但事实就是这样。

482
00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:36.030
So my group was reading Anna Karenina.
当时我们小组正在读《安娜·卡列尼娜》。

483
00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:39.530
You know, the classic novel about affairs and betrayal.
你知道的，那本关于出轨和背叛的经典小说。

484
00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:40.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

485
00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:51.110
Fitting because 10 minutes into one of our discussions, Olivia, my roommate, Jake's girlfriend, who would usually go for the wine, casually says,
很应景，因为讨论开始十分钟后，我室友杰克的女友奥利维亚，平时通常会去拿酒喝，随口说了句：

486
00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:53.710
Honestly, I don't even feel bad for Anna.
老实说，我甚至一点都不同情安娜。

487
00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:55.770
She knew exactly what she was doing.
她很清楚自己在做什么。

488
00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:59.530
Totally normal opinion, Lucas says.
卢卡斯说，这本是个很正常的观点。

489
00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:04.030
Except she says it while staring directly at our friend Zoe.
但她说这话时，正死死盯着我们的朋友佐伊。

490
00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.870
Zoe, immediately defensive, fires back, What is that supposed to mean?
佐伊立刻进入防御状态，反击道，你这话是什么意思？

491
00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:13.650
Olivia, smirking, says,
奥利维亚冷笑着说：

492
00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:14.530
Nothing.
没什么。

493
00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:18.050
Just that some people pretend they're innocent when they're not.
只是有些人明明不无辜，却装出一副无辜的样子。

494
00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:24.490
At this point, I didn't even know what was happening, but I definitely felt the tension.
那一刻，我甚至不知道发生了什么，但我确实感受到了紧张的气氛。

495
00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:29.770
Then Jake, who had been drinking as much wine as Olivia, just blurts out,
然后杰克，他喝的酒和奥利维亚一样多，突然脱口而出：

496
00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:32.750
Wait, is this about Zoe and Damien?
等等，这事儿跟佐伊和达米安有关吗？

497
00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:34.530
Who's Damien?
达米安是谁？

498
00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:35.410
Lucas writes.
卢卡斯写道。

499
00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:40.770
Now, Damien, who is also in the book club because he was good friends with Olivia,
而达米安，他也是读书俱乐部的成员，因为他和奥利维亚关系很好，

500
00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:44.150
had been scrolling his phone like he wasn't a part of the conversation,
他一直盯着手机，好像他根本没参与这场对话一样，

501
00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:46.430
and suddenly looks up, panicked.
突然抬头，一脸惊恐。

502
00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:52.010
Zoe goes white, and Bethany, Damien's actual girlfriend at the time,
佐伊脸色惨白，而当时正和达米安交往的贝瑟尼，

503
00:22:52.270 --> 00:22:54.550
just turns to him completely silent.
转过头看着他，一言不发。

504
00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:56.470
Lucas says,
卢卡斯说，

505
00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:57.930
Nobody is breathing.
大家连大气都不敢出。

506
00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:00.250
Zoe breaks first and says,
佐伊先沉不住气了，说道，

507
00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:02.050
Are you serious right now?
你是认真的吗？

508
00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:03.550
Damien says,
达米安说，

509
00:23:03.930 --> 00:23:05.970
I don't—what are you guys talking about?
我没……你们在说什么啊？

510
00:23:07.830 --> 00:23:12.190
Olivia, enjoying every second of this, just shrugs while looking at Zoe again.
奥利维亚很享受这一刻，她耸了耸肩，再次看向佐伊。

511
00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:13.330
Oh, nothing.
哦，没什么。

512
00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:15.990
Just that some people don't respect boundaries.
只是有些人不懂得尊重界限。

513
00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:17.710
You know, like Anna.
你知道的，就像安娜那样。

514
00:23:18.230 --> 00:23:19.410
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

515
00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:22.490
And then, the plot twist that ends everything,
然后，终结一切的剧情反转来了，

516
00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:25.150
Zoe turns to Damien and says,
佐伊转向达米安说，

517
00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:26.410
You told her?
你告诉她了？

518
00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:27.850
Boom.
砰。

519
00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:29.190
Nuclear explosion.
核弹爆炸。

520
00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:30.990
Bethany stands up and leaves.
贝瑟尼起身离开。

521
00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:31.970
Doesn't say a word.
一句话也没说。

522
00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:33.510
Zoe storms after her.
佐伊气冲冲地追了出去。

523
00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:36.110
Damien just sits there, fully deceased.
达米安坐在那儿，彻底凉了。

524
00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.590
Olivia sips her wine, pleased.
奥利维亚抿了一口酒，心满意足。

525
00:23:38.590 --> 00:23:44.210
And then, because Jake cannot let the moment sit in silence, he just sighs and goes,
然后，因为杰克受不了这种沉默，他叹了口气说，

526
00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:47.290
So, are we still talking about the book?
所以，我们还在讨论那本书吗？

527
00:23:47.510 --> 00:23:48.110
Or?
还是说？

528
00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:50.190
No, Jake.
不，杰克。

529
00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:51.610
Clearly not.
显然不是。

530
00:23:52.210 --> 00:23:54.290
Anyway, book club is dead.
总之，读书会散伙了。

531
00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:55.970
Bethany broke up with Damien.
贝瑟尼和达米安分手了。

532
00:23:56.230 --> 00:23:58.030
Damien stopped being friends with Olivia.
达米安和奥利维亚绝交了。

533
00:23:58.030 --> 00:24:01.010
But at least Zoe and Damien are dating now.
但至少佐伊和达米安现在在一起了。

534
00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:01.710
Oh.
哦。

535
00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:05.090
I was lucky enough to not catch any strays.
我很幸运，没被卷进这场风波里。

536
00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:08.950
But one thing's for sure, nobody's ever reading Anna Karenina again.
但有一点是肯定的，再也没人会去读《安娜·卡列尼娜》了。

537
00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:11.270
Wow.
哇。

538
00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:12.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

539
00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:13.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

540
00:24:13.510 --> 00:24:15.770
That's a spicy book club story.
这读书会的故事真够劲爆的。

541
00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:20.820
Angela, have you ever been in a book club?
安吉拉，你参加过读书会吗？

542
00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.180
And did it have drama?
里面有发生过什么抓马的事吗？

543
00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.420
I mean, no.
这个嘛，没有。

544
00:24:24.760 --> 00:24:26.040
I've never been asked.
从来没人邀请过我。

545
00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:27.100
Here's the thing.
是这样的。

546
00:24:27.200 --> 00:24:29.400
I have several friends in different book clubs.
我有几个朋友在不同的读书会里。

547
00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:31.160
And I've never been invited.
但我从来没被邀请过。

548
00:24:31.360 --> 00:24:32.920
And it does not bump me at all.
我一点也不难过。

549
00:24:33.020 --> 00:24:33.720
It really doesn't.
真的不难过。

550
00:24:33.720 --> 00:24:36.900
I mean, I just have always thought, well, when the timing's right, it'll happen.
我是说，我一直觉得，时机到了，自然就会有的。

551
00:24:37.120 --> 00:24:41.880
And honestly, I don't have any free time right now with, like, all the kids and extracurricular
说实话，我现在根本没空，因为要照顾孩子，还有各种课外

552
00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:42.360
activities.
活动。

553
00:24:42.360 --> 00:24:46.480
I'm like, I don't know when I'd be going to this book club or hosting a book club.
我不知道自己什么时候能去参加或者举办读书会。

554
00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:55.540
But I do have a friend that is very miffed that she isn't in this one particular book
但我有个朋友，她因为没能加入某个特定的读书会而感到非常

555
00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:55.840
club.
恼火。

556
00:24:56.480 --> 00:25:01.760
And whenever we get together with this group of gals for other things, it's just me and
每当我们这群姐妹聚在一起做别的事情时，就只有我和

557
00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:03.260
her that's not in the book club.
她没参加那个读书会。

558
00:25:03.380 --> 00:25:04.680
But I don't care.
但我不在乎。

559
00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:05.820
I don't care.
我真的不在乎。

560
00:25:06.340 --> 00:25:11.680
And sometimes when we're all together, they will bring up a book they're reading or who
有时我们聚在一起，她们会提起正在读的书，或者谁

561
00:25:11.680 --> 00:25:16.560
hosted or how late their book club went that night or, oh, my gosh, that, you know, whatever,
做东，或者那天读书会聚到多晚，或者，天哪，那个，你知道，不管是什么，

562
00:25:16.720 --> 00:25:21.160
that gluten-free lemon tart you made was so good or what, some little tidbit from the
你做的那个无麸质柠檬塔真好吃，或者诸如此类，关于

563
00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:21.680
book club.
读书会的一些小道消息。

564
00:25:21.940 --> 00:25:25.000
And she literally is, like, seething.
她简直气得火冒三丈。

565
00:25:25.300 --> 00:25:27.060
Well, because that's tacky.
嗯，因为那样做很没品。

566
00:25:27.260 --> 00:25:28.060
Well, I don't.
好吧，我倒不觉得。

567
00:25:28.060 --> 00:25:29.340
I'm sorry to say.
很抱歉这么说。

568
00:25:29.520 --> 00:25:34.380
Who are these women who are, like, actively talking about their little club in front of
到底是什么样的女人，会在两个没加入她们俱乐部的人面前

569
00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:36.100
two people who aren't in their club?
大谈特谈她们的小圈子？

570
00:25:36.100 --> 00:25:37.280
Well, I don't care.
嗯，我不在乎。

571
00:25:37.580 --> 00:25:41.320
It's like, this book club has been going for years before I was even in this.
就像这个读书会，在我加入这个圈子之前就已经存在好多年了。

572
00:25:41.680 --> 00:25:42.860
Like, circle of people.
就是这个圈子。

573
00:25:43.460 --> 00:25:48.720
But anyway, what kind of tickles me is the other gal that's not in it.
但不管怎样，让我觉得好笑的是另一个没加入的姑娘。

574
00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:54.620
Now, just really, if anyone's paying attention, she does things like she goes, ugh, or she
现在，真的，如果有人注意的话，她会做出一些举动，比如发出“呃”的声音，或者

575
00:25:54.620 --> 00:25:57.340
rolls for us when they talk about their club.
当她们谈论俱乐部时，她会翻白眼。

576
00:25:57.580 --> 00:25:58.020
Yes.
没错。

577
00:25:58.380 --> 00:26:00.800
Anyway, it just kind of cracks me up.
总之，这让我觉得挺逗的。

578
00:26:00.940 --> 00:26:02.160
And I'm just like, I don't know.
我只是觉得，我不知道。

579
00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:06.660
Book clubs seem like a lot of, like, maintenance, like emotional maintenance.
读书会似乎需要很多维护，比如情感上的维护。

580
00:26:07.120 --> 00:26:09.140
I've been in two book clubs.
我参加过两个读书会。

581
00:26:09.620 --> 00:26:11.480
They both ended in disaster.
最后都以灾难收场。

582
00:26:11.680 --> 00:26:12.980
Oh, my gosh!
天哪！

583
00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:18.800
One of them, the first one I was in, I got invited to, and it was a very similar thing
其中一个，我参加的第一个，我是受邀加入的，情况和你朋友的

584
00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:23.140
as your friend, which is that this was, like, a group of women that were all really good
很像，那是一群关系非常好的女性朋友，

585
00:26:23.140 --> 00:26:25.520
friends, and they, like, vacationed together.
她们经常一起去度假。

586
00:26:25.860 --> 00:26:31.800
And there was, like, me and one other gal who were not invited on the vacations.
当时我和另一个姑娘没被邀请去度假。

587
00:26:32.140 --> 00:26:35.800
And I didn't care, because honestly, I didn't want to vacation with them.
我不在乎，因为说实话，我也不想和她们一起度假。

588
00:26:35.800 --> 00:26:38.840
But I didn't know them, you know?
但我又不认识她们，你懂吗？

589
00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:44.500
But, like, a good portion of the book club meeting would be taken up with making these
但是，读书会很大一部分时间都被用来制定这些

590
00:26:44.500 --> 00:26:44.960
plans.
计划了。

591
00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:50.040
And I just sort of felt like, I just want to talk about the book.
我当时就觉得，我只想聊聊书。

592
00:26:50.220 --> 00:26:50.640
Right.
没错。

593
00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:52.940
I don't need to talk about everyone's vacation.
我不需要讨论大家的度假计划。

594
00:26:52.940 --> 00:26:56.660
But I get it because this is the time they're all together, and they can all look at their
但我理解，因为这是她们聚在一起的时间，她们可以查看

595
00:26:56.660 --> 00:27:00.920
calendars, and they can all figure out where they want to go this summer or whatever for
日历，可以商量今年夏天想去哪里，或者为她们的

596
00:27:00.920 --> 00:27:01.760
their girls' trip.
闺蜜之旅做打算。

597
00:27:02.480 --> 00:27:04.520
I found it annoying for that reason.
因为这个原因，我觉得很烦。

598
00:27:04.840 --> 00:27:09.920
But then some drama happened from one of the vacations, and it ended up blowing up the
后来其中一次度假发生了一些矛盾，结果导致

599
00:27:09.920 --> 00:27:10.400
whole book club.
整个读书会彻底散伙了。

600
00:27:10.520 --> 00:27:11.360
I don't even know what happened.
我甚至都不知道发生了什么。

601
00:27:11.420 --> 00:27:12.760
I wasn't very good friends with them.
我和他们关系不太好。

602
00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:18.180
This was, like, when I first moved to L.A., and I got sort of invited in, and I just needed
那大概是我刚搬到洛杉矶的时候，我算是被邀请加入的，我当时只是需要

603
00:27:18.180 --> 00:27:18.980
something to do.
找点事情做。

604
00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:21.760
I thought I was going to meet people, maybe make some friends.
我以为我能认识些人，也许能交到几个朋友。

605
00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:22.980
It did not work out.
结果事与愿违。

606
00:27:23.220 --> 00:27:27.660
Well, the other thing I'm kind of learning by being the person not invited in the book
好吧，作为那个没被读书会邀请的人，我学到的另一件事是，人们一旦组建好

607
00:27:27.660 --> 00:27:35.140
club is that people are so—once they get their book club set, they are not taking any
读书会，他们就不会再接受任何

608
00:27:35.140 --> 00:27:35.900
applications.
申请了。

609
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:36.580
No.
没错。

610
00:27:37.020 --> 00:27:38.160
Like, that's it.
就是这样。

611
00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:41.780
If you have a successful book club, you don't want to mess with the chemistry.
如果你有一个成功的读书会，你肯定不想破坏那种化学反应。

612
00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:43.720
That's why my feelings aren't hurt.
所以我一点也不难过。

613
00:27:43.860 --> 00:27:46.740
Who knows what I'd bring into it, you know?
谁知道我会给他们带去什么影响呢，对吧？

614
00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:48.560
Also, we got this one letter.
另外，我们收到了一封信。

615
00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:51.700
Now, this isn't the one that I said, don't read, okay?
这封信可不是我之前说“别读”的那封，好吗？

616
00:27:52.160 --> 00:27:54.140
But I was curious about this letter.
但我对这封信很好奇。

617
00:27:54.660 --> 00:27:57.340
Do you have to pay dues to be in some book clubs?
有些读书会需要交会费吗？

618
00:27:57.660 --> 00:27:58.680
Is that a thing?
有这种事吗？

619
00:27:58.820 --> 00:27:59.860
Listen to this letter, okay?
听听这封信，好吗？

620
00:28:00.060 --> 00:28:00.300
Okay.
好的。

621
00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:03.920
It's from Jim in Manchester, United Kingdom.
这是来自英国曼彻斯特的吉姆写的。

622
00:28:04.520 --> 00:28:05.940
