那我们两个每个月开车一小时的人怎么办？

1092
00:48:08.710 --> 00:48:14.430
For eight months, we have been driving to the book club on the west side.
八个月来，我们一直开车去西区参加读书会。

1093
00:48:14.430 --> 00:48:23.550
And in the car, as we would sit in traffic for this two-hour round-trip adventure, we would just say, you know what?
在车上，当我们堵在路上进行这趟两小时往返的旅程时，我们只会说，你知道吗？

1094
00:48:23.810 --> 00:48:25.310
Two months out of the year.
一年里也就这两个月。

1095
00:48:25.490 --> 00:48:26.390
We get it.
我们懂了。

1096
00:48:26.550 --> 00:48:28.710
We will not have to do the driving.
我们不用开车了。

1097
00:48:29.110 --> 00:48:30.030
So what happened?
那后来发生了什么？

1098
00:48:30.230 --> 00:48:31.550
Did they say, oh.
她们有没有说，哦。

1099
00:48:31.890 --> 00:48:32.610
Like, what did you say?
你是怎么说的？

1100
00:48:32.690 --> 00:48:33.870
You have to be like, it's our turn.
你得说，该轮到我们了。

1101
00:48:33.990 --> 00:48:34.530
It's our turn.
轮到我们了。

1102
00:48:34.530 --> 00:48:37.930
She said, I was really looking forward to hosting.
她说，我真的很期待这次由我来做东。

1103
00:48:38.030 --> 00:48:39.430
I've planned the menu.
我已经定好了菜单。

1104
00:48:39.770 --> 00:48:41.190
I've bought the food.
我已经买好了食材。

1105
00:48:41.330 --> 00:48:48.170
Because this suggestion of changing the location of the book club came in, like, the day before the book club was happening.
因为这个关于更换读书会地点的建议，是在读书会开始前一天才提出来的。

1106
00:48:48.170 --> 00:48:50.610
When she realized it wasn't on the west side.
当她意识到地点不在西区时。

1107
00:48:50.690 --> 00:48:50.990
Yes.
是的。

1108
00:48:51.150 --> 00:48:51.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1109
00:48:51.370 --> 00:48:54.690
So, my friend said, no.
所以，我的朋友说，不行。

1110
00:48:54.690 --> 00:48:56.710
I was really looking forward to hosting.
我真的很期待这次由我来做东。

1111
00:48:57.130 --> 00:48:58.730
I've planned the menu.
我已经定好了菜单。

1112
00:48:59.110 --> 00:49:00.610
It's going to be at my house.
读书会就在我家举行。

1113
00:49:01.290 --> 00:49:02.150
What happened?
后来怎么了？

1114
00:49:02.810 --> 00:49:04.990
Like, half the people didn't come.
结果，有一半的人没来。

1115
00:49:05.410 --> 00:49:05.790
Wow.
哇。

1116
00:49:06.310 --> 00:49:07.530
They didn't drive.
她们没开车过来。

1117
00:49:08.090 --> 00:49:13.290
So, like, six of you are just talking about this book, and the other six are just like, we're not driving there.
所以，你们六个人在讨论这本书，而另外六个人就觉得，我们才不要开车去那儿呢。

1118
00:49:13.570 --> 00:49:13.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1119
00:49:14.310 --> 00:49:17.270
They said, we're really sorry, but it was just, it's too much of a trek.
她们说，真的很抱歉，但那地方实在太远了。

1120
00:49:17.590 --> 00:49:19.170
What do they think you'd been doing?
她们以为你之前都在干嘛？

1121
00:49:19.750 --> 00:49:20.270
Exactly!
就是说啊！

1122
00:49:20.270 --> 00:49:20.410
Really?
真的吗？

1123
00:49:21.090 --> 00:49:21.550
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1124
00:49:21.650 --> 00:49:22.550
Exactly, lady.
就是说啊，大姐。

1125
00:49:22.890 --> 00:49:23.230
Nope.
没门。

1126
00:49:24.050 --> 00:49:24.830
We quit.
我们退出了。

1127
00:49:25.210 --> 00:49:25.870
You quit?
你们退出了？

1128
00:49:26.130 --> 00:49:27.310
Me and my valley friend.
我和我那位山谷地区的朋友。

1129
00:49:27.530 --> 00:49:28.950
Did you start a valley book club?
你们自己组建了一个山谷读书会吗？

1130
00:49:29.210 --> 00:49:30.030
We didn't.
没有。

1131
00:49:30.870 --> 00:49:32.610
We just were like, you know what?
我们当时就想，你知道吗？

1132
00:49:32.690 --> 00:49:33.090
We're done.
我们受够了。

1133
00:49:33.530 --> 00:49:34.830
It was too much.
这太过分了。

1134
00:49:34.990 --> 00:49:35.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
00:49:35.070 --> 00:49:36.630
It was such a slap in the face.
这简直是当众打脸。

1136
00:49:36.830 --> 00:49:37.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1137
00:49:38.130 --> 00:49:38.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1138
00:49:38.790 --> 00:49:40.910
I was going to say, are you still friends with that group?
我正想问，你还和那个小组的人是朋友吗？

1139
00:49:41.050 --> 00:49:41.870
You know, no.
说实话，没有了。

1140
00:49:42.130 --> 00:49:46.610
None of, I'm still friends with the gal from the west side.
除了那位西区的朋友，其他人我都不联系了。

1141
00:49:46.730 --> 00:49:49.570
She's actually moved away, so I don't see her very much.
她其实已经搬走了，所以我也不怎么见她。

1142
00:49:49.690 --> 00:49:49.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1143
00:49:49.990 --> 00:49:53.130
But I'm kept in touch with zero of the other ladies.
但其他那些女士，我一个都没再联系过。

1144
00:49:53.770 --> 00:49:54.490
Here's the thing.
关键是这样。

1145
00:49:54.790 --> 00:49:57.310
As you know, I have never been invited to be in a book club.
如你所知，我从来没被邀请参加过读书会。

1146
00:49:57.710 --> 00:50:01.430
But I am just seeing now all the shit comes out at book club.
但我现在才发现，读书会里全是破事儿。

1147
00:50:01.630 --> 00:50:01.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1148
00:50:02.270 --> 00:50:03.270
I had no idea.
我完全没想到。

1149
00:50:03.570 --> 00:50:07.650
I knew there was drama-ish, but I had no idea it was this amount.
我知道里面会有一些勾心斗角，但没想到会有这么多。

1150
00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:13.750
Speaking of book club drama, can I please share the letter I told you not to read now?
说到读书会的狗血剧情，我现在可以分享那封我让你别读的信了吗？

1151
00:50:13.870 --> 00:50:14.170
Yes.
是的。

1152
00:50:14.170 --> 00:50:14.710
Okay.
好的。

1153
00:50:14.930 --> 00:50:17.110
This letter is from Daphne B.
这封信来自蒙大拿州的达芙妮·B。

1154
00:50:17.450 --> 00:50:18.490
in Montana.
来自蒙大拿州。

1155
00:50:19.190 --> 00:50:20.490
Daphne wrote in and said,
达芙妮写信来说，

1156
00:50:21.070 --> 00:50:25.470
I am part of a book club that has a main group of girls and then some other ladies.
我参加了一个读书俱乐部，里面有一个核心成员小组，还有一些其他女士。

1157
00:50:25.470 --> 00:50:34.270
It's usually like 15-ish girls, and every month, 10 to 12 show up, and it's a super great time and a fun way to get some girl time.
通常有15个左右的女孩，每个月会有10到12个人参加，大家玩得很开心，也是一种享受闺蜜时光的有趣方式。

1158
00:50:34.670 --> 00:50:42.010
Well, one of the main girls texted our big chat that she wasn't going to be part of the book club anymore, which shocked me.
结果，其中一个核心成员在我们的群聊里发消息说她不再参加读书俱乐部了，这让我很震惊。

1159
00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:43.470
Shocked in all caps.
是大写加粗的震惊。

1160
00:50:43.870 --> 00:50:45.570
So I knew something was wrong.
所以我知道出事了。

1161
00:50:46.070 --> 00:50:48.370
At the next book club, I got the tea.
在下一次读书会时，我打听到了内幕。

1162
00:50:49.350 --> 00:50:52.570
Apparently, the girl that left the club, let's call her Lucy.
显然，那个退出俱乐部的女孩，我们叫她露西吧。

1163
00:50:52.910 --> 00:50:54.150
You know we love it.
你知道我们最爱这个了。

1164
00:50:54.150 --> 00:50:54.590
We love this.
我们太爱这个了。

1165
00:50:54.670 --> 00:50:55.990
When we have to have a code name.
当我们不得不使用代号的时候。

1166
00:50:56.070 --> 00:50:57.370
Please give us all the code names.
请务必给我们所有的代号。

1167
00:50:57.830 --> 00:50:58.270
Okay.
好的。

1168
00:50:58.470 --> 00:51:01.130
So apparently the girl that left the club, let's call her Lucy,
所以显然那个退出俱乐部的女孩，我们叫她露西，

1169
00:51:01.410 --> 00:51:10.990
was because all the other main group of friends had confronted her as an entire group because Lucy and her husband and another girl from the book club
是因为其他核心朋友圈的人集体质问了她，因为露西和她丈夫，还有读书俱乐部里的另一个女孩，

1170
00:51:11.890 --> 00:51:14.890
that is also not a part of the main friend group.
那个女孩也不属于核心朋友圈。

1171
00:51:14.950 --> 00:51:16.310
Let's call her Hannah.
我们叫她汉娜吧。

1172
00:51:16.610 --> 00:51:16.970
Okay.
好的。

1173
00:51:17.650 --> 00:51:19.390
They all got it on.
他们全都搞在了一起。

1174
00:51:19.790 --> 00:51:20.130
Wait.
等等。

1175
00:51:20.810 --> 00:51:24.270
Hannah, Lucy, and Lucy's husband had a threesome.
汉娜、露西和露西的丈夫玩了三人行。

1176
00:51:24.430 --> 00:51:24.950
Yes.
是的。

1177
00:51:25.190 --> 00:51:27.870
But Hannah and Lucy are in the book club together.
但汉娜和露西都在同一个读书俱乐部里。

1178
00:51:28.130 --> 00:51:28.790
They were.
她们曾经是。

1179
00:51:29.810 --> 00:51:33.310
She goes on to say, Hannah had already left the group.
她接着说，汉娜已经退出了小组。

1180
00:51:33.690 --> 00:51:37.150
And then in parentheses, she said she only ever came to a few book clubs.
然后在括号里，她说汉娜只来过几次读书会。

1181
00:51:37.150 --> 00:51:42.750
But Lucy was confronted about her husband being the worst and how she should leave him.
但露西被质问了，因为她丈夫是个渣男，大家劝她离开他。

1182
00:51:43.410 --> 00:51:45.810
The whole group confronted her.
整个小组都去质问她了。

1183
00:51:47.790 --> 00:51:51.010
Well, mind you, this made me laugh.
嗯，提醒一下，这让我笑了。

1184
00:51:51.890 --> 00:51:57.410
Mind you, this book club is filled with a bunch of what I thought to be vanilla married ladies.
提醒一下，这个读书俱乐部里满是我以为的那种平淡无奇的已婚女士。

1185
00:51:57.630 --> 00:51:59.570
And a lot have young kids.
而且很多人都有年幼的孩子。

1186
00:52:00.310 --> 00:52:06.210
Well, Lucy chose to stand by her man and now isn't talking to anyone in the group and told them all off.
好吧，露西选择支持她的丈夫，现在不和小组里的任何人说话，还把她们都骂了一顿。

1187
00:52:06.990 --> 00:52:08.570
Daphne wraps it up by saying,
达芙妮在结尾说，

1188
00:52:09.010 --> 00:52:13.310
I am a mom of a little one and this book club has been a fun way for me to get out of the house
我是一个小宝宝的妈妈，这个读书俱乐部一直是我走出家门的一种有趣方式，

1189
00:52:13.310 --> 00:52:15.450
and have some adult time one evening a month.
每个月能有一个晚上享受成年人的时光。

1190
00:52:15.630 --> 00:52:17.690
And I love the good fantasy books.
而且我喜欢那些精彩的奇幻小说。

1191
00:52:17.990 --> 00:52:20.330
Side note, Angela would love our books.
顺便提一下，安吉拉一定会喜欢我们的书。

1192
00:52:21.550 --> 00:52:24.010
But this whole situation is awkward now.
但现在整个局面变得很尴尬。

1193
00:52:24.090 --> 00:52:28.550
And I'm so happy I wasn't involved and was completely clueless about the whole situation.
我很庆幸自己没有卷入其中，对整件事完全一无所知。

1194
00:52:28.870 --> 00:52:30.350
So what do you think, office ladies?
那么你们怎么看，办公室女士们？

1195
00:52:30.590 --> 00:52:34.770
Should I stick out the awkwardness now that I know or should I leave?
既然我已经知道了，我是该忍受这种尴尬继续待下去，还是应该离开？

1196
00:52:34.770 --> 00:52:36.430
And that's the tea.
这就是全部内幕了。

1197
00:52:37.150 --> 00:52:37.450
Well.
嗯。

1198
00:52:37.890 --> 00:52:41.910
I mean, Lucy has told this whole group to F off.
我的意思是，露西已经让整个小组滚蛋了。

1199
00:52:42.170 --> 00:52:42.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1200
00:52:43.050 --> 00:52:44.450
Hannah's not coming anymore.
汉娜也不会再来了。

1201
00:52:44.690 --> 00:52:49.430
I mean, listen, the two problems in this story are not at the book club anymore.
我是说，听着，这个故事里的两个问题已经不在读书俱乐部里了。

1202
00:52:49.650 --> 00:52:50.490
That is true.
确实如此。

1203
00:52:50.910 --> 00:52:51.790
That is true.
确实如此。

1204
00:52:51.890 --> 00:52:53.990
I guess you just have to wonder, though.
不过我想你还是会忍不住好奇。

1205
00:52:54.410 --> 00:52:56.270
When are they going to turn on someone else?
她们什么时候会把矛头转向别人呢？

1206
00:52:56.310 --> 00:52:56.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1207
00:52:56.710 --> 00:53:00.570
Are they going to meddle in someone else's marriage and personal lives?
她们会去干涉别人的婚姻和私生活吗？

1208
00:53:00.570 --> 00:53:03.390
Have a group meeting to tell you your husband's the worst?
还要开个小组会议告诉你，你丈夫是世界上最糟糕的人？

1209
00:53:04.150 --> 00:53:04.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1210
00:53:05.010 --> 00:53:10.030
Well, I mean, there's two ladies who didn't think he was the worSt.
嗯，我是说，还有两位女士不觉得他是最糟糕的。

1211
00:53:10.250 --> 00:53:10.730
Apparently.
显然是这样。

1212
00:53:11.070 --> 00:53:11.230
Right.
没错。

1213
00:53:11.730 --> 00:53:14.850
But also, like, do book clubs always get that personal?
但话说回来，读书俱乐部总是这么私人化吗？

1214
00:53:16.090 --> 00:53:21.230
Lady, I know we're getting ready to wrap it up, but I actually have one more letter.
女士，我知道我们准备要结束了，但我其实还有一封信。

1215
00:53:21.750 --> 00:53:22.230
Okay.
好的。

1216
00:53:22.410 --> 00:53:24.750
Funny you should ask if they get personal.
你问得真巧，问她们是不是总是这么私人化。

1217
00:53:24.750 --> 00:53:28.590
This letter made me chuckle, and it made me think of Phyllis.
这封信让我忍俊不禁，也让我想起了菲利斯。

1218
00:53:29.410 --> 00:53:30.170
Our Phyllis?
我们的菲利斯？

1219
00:53:30.310 --> 00:53:32.430
Our Phyllis Lapp in Vance.
万斯的菲利斯·拉普。

1220
00:53:32.610 --> 00:53:32.890
Okay.
好的。

1221
00:53:34.590 --> 00:53:37.930
It's from Natalie P in Nashville, Tennessee, who said,
这是来自田纳西州纳什维尔的娜塔莉·P写的，她说：

1222
00:53:38.070 --> 00:53:40.930
Years ago, our book club read Fifty Shades of Grey.
几年前，我们的读书俱乐部读了《五十度灰》。

1223
00:53:41.190 --> 00:53:41.650
Oh.
哦。

1224
00:53:42.330 --> 00:53:46.250
I remember my friend recommending it, and everyone in the room looked uneasy.
我记得我朋友推荐它的时候，房间里的每个人看起来都很不安。

1225
00:53:46.790 --> 00:53:51.230
I had not heard of it, so I spoke up and naively and energetically said,
我当时没听说过这本书，所以我天真又充满活力地开口说：

1226
00:53:51.290 --> 00:53:52.110
Yeah, let's do it.
好啊，我们就读这本吧。

1227
00:53:52.130 --> 00:53:53.130
It's your choice.
这是你的选择。

1228
00:53:54.810 --> 00:53:55.610
Natalie said,
娜塔莉说：

1229
00:53:55.730 --> 00:54:00.550
I bought the book, luckily on my iPad, because I brought it to school to read during lunch.
我买了这本书，幸好是在iPad上买的，因为我把它带到学校午休时看。

1230
00:54:00.730 --> 00:54:02.070
I'm a high school teacher.
我是一名高中老师。

1231
00:54:02.530 --> 00:54:05.510
Now I know why you said it makes you think of Phyllis Vance.
现在我知道你为什么说这让你想起万斯的菲利斯了。

1232
00:54:07.130 --> 00:54:13.870
And Natalie said, a few chapters in, I was horrified of what I was reading in broad daylight.
娜塔莉接着说，读了几章之后，我被自己在光天化日之下读的内容吓坏了。

1233
00:54:15.590 --> 00:54:24.690
So Natalie said, anyway, in a group of about—this is the part that cracked me up—in a group of about 12 ladies, eight of us got pregnant.
所以娜塔莉说，总之，在一个大约——这部分让我笑喷了——在一个大约12人的女士小组里，我们有8个人怀孕了。

1234
00:54:27.050 --> 00:54:32.890
The book club fell apart, and my husband likes to call the kids the gravies.
读书俱乐部解散了，我丈夫喜欢把这些孩子称为“意外之喜”。

1235
00:54:37.510 --> 00:54:39.550
That is fantastic.
这太棒了。

1236
00:54:39.990 --> 00:54:42.010
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1237
00:54:42.670 --> 00:54:47.150
Well, everyone, that was our Finer Things Club.
好了，各位，以上就是我们的“精致事物俱乐部”。

1238
00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:55.690
We had so much fun prepping this episode, doing this episode, hearing from you about your snooty clubs.
我们准备这期节目、录制这期节目，以及听你们分享那些势利俱乐部的事情，真的非常开心。

1239
00:54:55.690 --> 00:54:58.370
It was just a delight, start to finish.
从头到尾都让人愉悦。

1240
00:54:58.630 --> 00:55:00.510
This whole work week was so fun.
整个工作周都太有趣了。

1241
00:55:00.730 --> 00:55:01.170
I know.
我知道。

1242
00:55:01.230 --> 00:55:03.370
Culminating in our tea party with Sam and Cassie.
最后还有我们和萨姆、卡西的茶话会。

1243
00:55:03.570 --> 00:55:09.550
And lady, you know, when we originally broke down Branch Wars, we said we were going to start our own Finer Things Club.
女士，你知道，当我们最初拆解《分部战争》那集时，我们说过要成立自己的“精致事物俱乐部”。

1244
00:55:09.550 --> 00:55:11.970
We were going to read all the books that they read.
我们要读她们读过的所有书。

1245
00:55:12.090 --> 00:55:12.850
I remember.
我记得。

1246
00:55:12.850 --> 00:55:18.690
We never did it, but honestly, I think it's because I don't have a huge interest in the books that they read.
我们从来没做过，但老实说，我觉得是因为我对她们读的那些书没什么太大的兴趣。

1247
00:55:18.810 --> 00:55:21.570
But I would do a Finer Things Club with you.
但我愿意和你一起办个“精致事物俱乐部”。

1248
00:55:21.630 --> 00:55:22.790
Do you remember talking about this?
你还记得我们谈过这个吗？

1249
00:55:22.790 --> 00:55:23.170
I do.
我记得。

1250
00:55:23.170 --> 00:55:23.730
I do.
我记得。

1251
00:55:23.850 --> 00:55:27.230
And you actually said we could call it Finer's Things Club because—
而且你真的说我们可以把它叫作“更精致事物俱乐部”，因为——

1252
00:55:27.230 --> 00:55:27.710
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

1253
00:55:27.930 --> 00:55:29.690
Because I can never say it correctly.
因为我总是说不对这个名字。

1254
00:55:29.850 --> 00:55:36.290
And I want you to know the mental focus I have had to have every time we have said it in this episode.
而且我想让你知道，这集里每次提到这个名字时，我得有多么专注。

1255
00:55:36.290 --> 00:55:37.210
You did great.
你做得很好。

1256
00:55:37.210 --> 00:55:43.330
Well, I stumbled once or twice, but I really had to say Finer Things Club.
嗯，我磕巴了一两次，但我真的得说出“更精致事物俱乐部”这个名字。

1257
00:55:43.330 --> 00:55:44.790
I had to think about it.
我得好好琢磨一下。

1258
00:55:45.190 --> 00:55:51.110
And, you know, last time we shared that there was a blooper of me doing this, but we didn't play it.
而且，你知道，上次我们提到我有个说错名字的NG片段，但我们没放出来。

1259
00:55:51.290 --> 00:55:54.090
And a lot of people were like, you should play the blooper.
很多人都说，你们应该放那个NG片段。

1260
00:55:54.390 --> 00:55:55.210
Do you have it?
你有吗？

1261
00:55:55.350 --> 00:55:56.250
I have it.
我有。

1262
00:55:56.350 --> 00:55:57.470
Oh, you have to play.
噢，你一定要放出来。

1263
00:55:57.470 --> 00:55:58.250
I want to hear it.
我想听听。

1264
00:55:58.570 --> 00:55:58.650
Okay.
好的。

1265
00:55:59.590 --> 00:56:04.450
No problem with the Finer Things Club, but the Finer's Thing—
说“更精致事物俱乐部”没问题，但“更精致的……”

1266
00:56:08.030 --> 00:56:08.990
The Finer's—
“更精致的……”

1267
00:56:11.710 --> 00:56:13.090
The Finer's—
“更精致的……”

1268
00:56:15.190 --> 00:56:16.870
The Finer's Things Club.
“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1269
00:56:17.090 --> 00:56:18.010
The Finer's Things Club.
“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1270
00:56:18.250 --> 00:56:18.550
Okay.
好吧。

1271
00:56:20.190 --> 00:56:21.150
The Finer's—
“更精致的……”

1272
00:56:23.020 --> 00:56:26.000
Well, lady, I will start the Finer's Things Club with you.
好吧，女士，我愿意和你一起创办“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1273
00:56:26.100 --> 00:56:28.000
It's hard for me to say Finer's Things.
对我来说说出“更精致事物”真的很难。

1274
00:56:28.200 --> 00:56:29.220
Finer's Things Club.
“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1275
00:56:29.220 --> 00:56:30.860
But I'll start that club with you.
但我愿意和你一起创办那个俱乐部。

1276
00:56:31.080 --> 00:56:33.020
But I just—I don't know.
但我只是——我不知道。

1277
00:56:33.020 --> 00:56:40.380
What if our Finer's Things Club is just going around and having tea at different places and going to art museums?
如果我们的“更精致事物俱乐部”只是到处喝喝下午茶、逛逛艺术博物馆呢？

1278
00:56:40.480 --> 00:56:42.180
That is absolutely fine with me.
我完全没意见。

1279
00:56:42.180 --> 00:56:44.340
You don't even have to read any books if you don't want to.
如果你不想的话，甚至连书都不用读。

1280
00:56:44.500 --> 00:56:49.900
Well, if history has taught us anything today, it's that you start a book club with people and it falls apart.
嗯，如果说今天历史教会了我们什么，那就是你和别人办读书俱乐部，最后总是会散伙。

1281
00:56:50.120 --> 00:56:50.340
Yeah.
没错。

1282
00:56:50.480 --> 00:56:52.820
And they feel like relationships implode.
而且感觉人际关系都会崩塌。

1283
00:56:53.200 --> 00:56:53.860
It's true.
确实如此。

1284
00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:55.560
So we can't start one.
所以我们不能办那个。

1285
00:56:55.920 --> 00:57:00.960
We also remember we're going to start an office ladies movie club that we never did as well.
我们也记得我们还打算办一个“办公室女士电影俱乐部”，结果也没办成。

1286
00:57:00.960 --> 00:57:01.480
Okay.
好吧。

1287
00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:05.720
Well, I like this idea of tea and art, museums, and movies.
嗯，我喜欢喝茶、看艺术、逛博物馆和看电影这个主意。

1288
00:57:06.060 --> 00:57:06.560
Great.
太棒了。

1289
00:57:06.860 --> 00:57:08.180
The Finer's Things Club.
“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1290
00:57:08.400 --> 00:57:09.720
The Finer's Things Club.
“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1291
00:57:10.220 --> 00:57:12.480
And we'll leave that book drama at the door.
我们就把那些关于书的闹剧拒之门外吧。

1292
00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:13.600
Okay.
好的。

1293
00:57:13.860 --> 00:57:16.720
Before we go, I have one last thing I want to share.
在结束之前，我还有最后一件事想分享。

1294
00:57:16.940 --> 00:57:21.060
I thought it might be a fun way to end this episode since we started with Andy.
我觉得这可能是结束本集的一种有趣方式，毕竟我们是从安迪开始聊起的。

1295
00:57:21.860 --> 00:57:28.060
There is a deleted scene where we learn Andy's fate about joining the Finer's Things Club.
有一个删减片段，里面交代了安迪申请加入“更精致事物俱乐部”的最终结果。

1296
00:57:28.440 --> 00:57:29.280
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

1297
00:57:32.930 --> 00:57:38.990
Dear Andrew Bernard, after carefully examining your application to the Finer's Things Club, we are unable to offer you a position at this place in time.
亲爱的安德鲁·伯纳德，在仔细审阅了你对“更精致事物俱乐部”的申请后，我们很遗憾目前无法为你提供名额。

1298
00:57:39.230 --> 00:57:45.610
We would, however, like to place you on a list in case an opportunity arises when your inclusion could be tolerated.
不过，我们想把你列入候补名单，以防未来出现能容忍你加入的机会。

1299
00:57:45.810 --> 00:57:49.750
Your position as an ongoing financial patron, however, is yours to cherish.
然而，你作为长期赞助人的身份，依然值得你珍惜。

1300
00:57:50.750 --> 00:57:52.870
Sincerely, the Finer's Things Club.
诚挚的，“更精致事物俱乐部”。

1301
00:57:53.450 --> 00:57:53.930
Yes!
太棒了！

1302
00:57:54.850 --> 00:57:55.330
Woohoo!
呜呼！

1303
00:57:56.170 --> 00:57:57.010
Weight listed!
候补名单！

1304
00:57:59.980 --> 00:58:00.900
So excited!
太激动了！

1305
00:58:01.300 --> 00:58:04.780
And you see Pam and Toby and Oscar over at Front Reception.
你看到帕姆、托比和奥斯卡在前台那边。

1306
00:58:04.780 --> 00:58:06.420
They're watching him open this letter.
他们正在看他拆这封信。

1307
00:58:06.580 --> 00:58:06.840
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1308
00:58:06.840 --> 00:58:07.740
It's really funny.
真的很有趣。

1309
00:58:08.140 --> 00:58:10.220
Aw, wait listed for the Finer's Things Club.
噢，进了“精品俱乐部”的候补名单。

1310
00:58:10.420 --> 00:58:11.180
It's perfect.
太完美了。

1311
00:58:11.580 --> 00:58:12.980
Well, thank you, everyone.
好吧，谢谢大家。

1312
00:58:13.420 --> 00:58:14.440
Thanks for writing in.
感谢你们的来信。

1313
00:58:14.560 --> 00:58:15.460
Thanks for listening today.
感谢大家今天的收听。

1314
00:58:15.460 --> 00:58:16.060
We love ya.
我们爱你们。

1315
00:58:16.220 --> 00:58:16.880
We love ya.
我们爱你们。

1316
00:58:16.940 --> 00:58:18.160
That was so much fun.
这太有趣了。

1317
00:58:18.160 --> 00:58:19.280
We hope you have a great week.
希望你们度过愉快的一周。

1318
00:58:19.560 --> 00:58:20.300
See you next week.
下周见。

1319
00:58:20.440 --> 00:58:20.900
See you then.
到时候见。

1320
00:58:20.900 --> 00:58:31.030
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

